WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.668
-I'm assuming you get asked
something that we get asked

00:00:01.668 --> 00:00:04.771
all the time, which is, "Does
Trump make your job easier?"

00:00:04.771 --> 00:00:06.006 line:92%
-Mm-hmm, yeah, which is --

00:00:06.006 --> 00:00:07.440 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's very hard
for people to understand

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.776 align:start size:94% position:6%
just how viscerally upsetting
that question is.

00:00:09.776 --> 00:00:12.012 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Because it doesn't.

00:00:12.012 --> 00:00:12.645 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
It makes it harder.

00:00:12.645 --> 00:00:14.447 size:84% position:42%
My wife, in the past,
has had to pull me away

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:16.583
from entirely well-meaning
people in the street, saying,

00:00:16.583 --> 00:00:19.019 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Well, I guess it just
writes itself, doesn't it?"

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.854 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'll say,
"I'll tell you whether

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:22.222 line:92%
it [bleep] writes itself or --

00:00:22.222 --> 00:00:24.124 line:92%
No, I'm talking to the lady!

00:00:24.124 --> 00:00:25.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
She wants to know
how easy it is.

00:00:25.525 --> 00:00:28.228 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll [bleep] tell her
how easy it is."

00:00:28.228 --> 00:00:28.895 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:00:28.895 --> 00:00:30.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
No, it's -- it's harder.
It's harder.

00:00:30.497 --> 00:00:35.035 align:start size:94% position:6%
Because, um, you know,
it's easy to do bad comedy,

00:00:35.035 --> 00:00:37.837 align:start size:94% position:6%
because you just
need to repeat what he says,

00:00:37.837 --> 00:00:39.139 size:81% position:41% line:92%
and that's not a joke.

00:00:39.139 --> 00:00:40.807 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's repetition.
-Yeah.

00:00:40.807 --> 00:00:42.742 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Whereas comedy,
especially if you want

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:45.545
to try and do something
that's not just happening

00:00:45.545 --> 00:00:47.781 align:start size:94% position:6%
online all the time,
is an effort.

00:00:47.781 --> 00:00:50.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'm not telling you something
you don't already feel

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:52.519 align:start size:94% position:6%
with every fiber
of your exhausted being.

00:00:52.519 --> 00:00:53.086 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:55.822 align:start size:94% position:6%
You do a lot of deep dives
on stories that are

00:00:55.822 --> 00:00:59.225
a little uncovered,
but you do spend a few minutes,

00:00:59.225 --> 00:01:01.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
I feel, like,
covering the Trump news

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:03.530 align:start size:94% position:6%
at the top of your show,
usually.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:05.565 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it seems like
you pick up --

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:06.266 size:88% position:44% line:92%
'Cause you go on Sunday,

00:01:06.266 --> 00:01:07.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
you kind of pick up
the end-of-the-week news.

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:10.937 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. So we literally started
thinking, at one point --

00:01:10.937 --> 00:01:11.971 size:81% position:41% line:92%
What time do you tape?

00:01:11.971 --> 00:01:14.707 size:78% position:39%
Because it's probably
about 5:30, right?

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:17.110
-We tape at 6:30, yeah, but
we're done at 5:30, yeah.

00:01:17.110 --> 00:01:19.813 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Exactly.
So, about 5:30 on a Thursday,

00:01:19.813 --> 00:01:23.950
at that point, you have dealt
with the fire-hosable [bleep]

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.151 line:92%
to the extent that you can,

00:01:25.151 --> 00:01:29.422
at which point the depressing
relay baton is put over to us.

00:01:29.422 --> 00:01:31.724 align:start size:94% position:6%
So, from Thursday
at 5:30 onwards,

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:35.895
it's our turn to open our mouth
and take that fire hose in.

00:01:35.895 --> 00:01:38.364 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:38.364 --> 00:01:40.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
Listen
to that revolted response.

00:01:40.166 --> 00:01:43.269 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Was that analogy necessary?"
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:43.269 --> 00:01:48.441 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, I want to speak about
another analogy of sorts.

00:01:48.441 --> 00:01:49.242 line:92%
This was a couple years ago.

00:01:49.242 --> 00:01:52.745
You said that America was
entering their Fat Elvis stage.

00:01:52.745 --> 00:01:54.380 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, that was more
than a couple of --

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:55.115 line:92%
That was a long time ago.

00:01:55.115 --> 00:01:56.583 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That was really --
It was a long time ago.

00:01:56.583 --> 00:01:58.885 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think that was pre-Obama.
-Wow.

00:01:58.885 --> 00:02:01.187
-The argument then
was saying that, yeah, exactly,

00:02:01.187 --> 00:02:04.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
you were kind of Elvis
in his Vegas years back then.

00:02:04.324 --> 00:02:05.892 align:start size:94% position:6%
Still objectively great...
-Yeah.

00:02:05.892 --> 00:02:08.695 align:start size:94% position:6%
-...but you could sense
the sadness coming.

00:02:08.695 --> 00:02:09.696 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:09.696 --> 00:02:11.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And that has really
kind of followed through.

00:02:11.865 --> 00:02:13.333 line:92%
-Well, it has followed through.

00:02:13.333 --> 00:02:15.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
'Cause at that point,
I thought that was as silly

00:02:15.902 --> 00:02:18.171
as it could get, and that
now seems a quaint idea,

00:02:18.171 --> 00:02:20.974
because I don't know what period
of Elvis you're in right now,

00:02:20.974 --> 00:02:23.910
but I think he's about to reach
for the flusher.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:25.044 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:25.044 --> 00:02:28.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Or we've now gone past --
This is --

00:02:28.381 --> 00:02:30.250 line:92%
In our analogy, Elvis lived.

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:31.551 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I think that's right.
-Yeah.

00:02:31.551 --> 00:02:33.786
-That is the really positive way
to think about it

00:02:33.786 --> 00:02:36.322 align:start size:94% position:6%
is that Elvis faked his death,
and he's back,

00:02:36.322 --> 00:02:38.324 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's living a weird,
weird life.

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:39.659 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-That's the Elvis you are now.

00:02:39.659 --> 00:02:41.761 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's weirder
than Vegas Elvis, yeah.

00:02:41.761 --> 00:02:43.229 line:92%
-So that is the perfect --

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:45.064 align:start size:94% position:6%
that is the perfect
distillation, I think,

00:02:45.064 --> 00:02:47.033 line:92%
of optimism and negativity.

00:02:47.033 --> 00:02:50.370 align:start size:94% position:6%
Negativity is,
"Elvis is dead now.

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.872 align:start size:94% position:6%
He died,
and he's dead forever."

00:02:52.872 --> 00:02:55.041 align:start size:94% position:6%
Optimism is,
"Elvis never died,

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:56.843 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he's about
to make a comeback album

00:02:56.843 --> 00:02:58.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
louder than ever before."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:58.978 --> 00:03:00.547 size:78% position:39%
-And it'll be, like,
"Is it the classics?"

00:03:00.547 --> 00:03:03.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
It's like, "No, it's crazy
new stuff that you..."

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:04.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
He's into drum --

00:03:04.417 --> 00:03:06.452 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's the balance is like,
"He's alive."

00:03:06.452 --> 00:03:07.187 size:78% position:39% line:92%
That's the good news.

00:03:07.187 --> 00:03:09.022 align:start size:94% position:6%
The bad news is,
it's crazier than ever.

00:03:09.022 --> 00:03:12.058
-He's like Sting.
He's really into lute music now.

00:03:12.058 --> 00:03:13.459 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.459 --> 00:03:14.928
-He's doing a live lute concert.
-That's right.

00:03:14.928 --> 00:03:17.564
And he's doing drum and bass.
He really likes drum and bass.

00:03:17.564 --> 00:03:19.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, good.
That's what Elvis needed.

00:03:19.399 --> 00:03:21.601 align:start size:94% position:6%
I do want to ask --
I forgot to ask this earlier,

00:03:21.601 --> 00:03:23.803 size:88% position:44%
because Beyoncé is also
in the "Lion King" film.

00:03:23.803 --> 00:03:25.605 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Whoo!
-Yes. That's right.

00:03:25.605 --> 00:03:27.040 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Cheers and applause ]
That's --

00:03:27.040 --> 00:03:30.777
That is the appropriate response
to the word "Beyoncé."

00:03:30.777 --> 00:03:31.911 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yeah.

00:03:31.911 --> 00:03:34.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And that's real-life royalty,
Beyoncé.

00:03:34.347 --> 00:03:36.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, gotcha.
So, have you met her?

00:03:36.449 --> 00:03:38.484 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I would drop
to my [bleep] knees.

00:03:38.484 --> 00:03:40.753 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, you would.
-Yeah.

00:03:40.753 --> 00:03:45.225 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:45.225 --> 00:03:47.393 align:start size:94% position:6%
Don't.
Please.

00:03:47.393 --> 00:03:49.796 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Don't look at me, Queen.

00:03:49.796 --> 00:03:51.297 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Don't look at me, Queen!

00:03:51.297 --> 00:03:53.933 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It is really --
She's a very hard person --

00:03:53.933 --> 00:03:54.567 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Have you met her?

00:03:54.567 --> 00:03:57.837
-Like, only in those very brief
"SNL" sort of, like,

00:03:57.837 --> 00:03:59.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
passing moments.
-That counts.

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:03.276 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It counts,
but it renders you wordless.

00:04:03.276 --> 00:04:05.411 line:92%
-Did she say hello to you?

00:04:05.411 --> 00:04:07.580 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-You met her!

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:04:10.984 --> 00:04:13.119 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I don't --
I don't care that you're sick.

00:04:13.119 --> 00:04:16.589 align:start size:94% position:6%
-All this stuff.
These were here.

00:04:16.589 --> 00:04:17.523 line:92%
-Two years ago, at the Emmys,

00:04:17.523 --> 00:04:19.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was supposed
to be sitting behind her,

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:20.426 size:84% position:42% line:92%
and she didn't turn up.

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:22.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
And my only plan
for the whole Emmys

00:04:22.161 --> 00:04:23.396 align:start size:94% position:6%
was to watch
the back of her head

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:26.132
and witness her interacting with
her immediate surroundings.

00:04:26.132 --> 00:04:29.836
-Yeah. With all due respect to
whoever is hosting the Emmys,

00:04:29.836 --> 00:04:31.938 align:start size:94% position:6%
nothing -- no one
has ever done it better

00:04:31.938 --> 00:04:33.072 line:92%
than the back of Beyoncé's head.

00:04:33.072 --> 00:04:33.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.973 --> 00:04:36.376 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, yeah, she's in
the "Lion King," as well,

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:37.377 size:88% position:44% line:92%
and I am absolutely sure

00:04:37.377 --> 00:04:39.512 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I will not
be allowed to meet her,

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:42.048
especially after this interview.
-No.

00:04:42.048 --> 00:04:44.717 align:start size:94% position:6%
-This feels like something
her security team

00:04:44.717 --> 00:04:46.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
should be made aware of
in some way.

00:04:46.819 --> 00:04:50.890
"He seems a little highly strung
when her name comes up."

00:04:50.890 --> 00:04:51.758 line:92%
-Your show's on a holiday break,

00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:56.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
but Catheter Cowboy
is gonna be in action.

00:04:56.362 --> 00:04:57.063 line:92%
For those who don't know,

00:04:57.063 --> 00:04:59.365
you want to give a quick
description of Catheter Cowboy?

00:04:59.365 --> 00:05:03.202 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, it's quite hard
to explain.

00:05:03.202 --> 00:05:06.773 align:start size:94% position:6%
But, basically, there is
a Catheter Cowboy on Fox News,

00:05:06.773 --> 00:05:10.143
and Fox News is obviously where
our current president

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:15.381
gets lots of information,
which is both fact and sad.

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:17.450 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so to try
and sneak information to him,

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:19.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
we've been taking out ads
on Fox News

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:20.720 line:92%
with our own Catheter Cowboy,

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:24.057
trying to explain to him things
like what the Nuclear Triad is.

00:05:24.057 --> 00:05:25.925 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-And so he will be --

00:05:25.925 --> 00:05:27.427 align:start size:94% position:6%
While we're away,
he will be appearing

00:05:27.427 --> 00:05:31.597
sporadically on Fox News,
trying to get information

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:33.099 line:92%
into his unyielding head.

00:05:33.099 --> 00:05:36.469
-And so these are ads that
you've shot and time bought.

00:05:36.469 --> 00:05:38.371 align:start size:94% position:6%
-That's right.
They will be --

00:05:38.371 --> 00:05:43.009
They will be getting rolled out
until they are stopped.

00:05:43.009 --> 00:05:43.743 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:05:43.743 --> 00:05:45.812 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's always
very difficult times

00:05:45.812 --> 00:05:47.246 line:92%
when you guys are on a break.

00:05:47.246 --> 00:05:47.947 size:75% position:38% line:92%
I hope you can rest,

00:05:47.947 --> 00:05:49.449 align:start size:94% position:6%
although I know you guys
rarely do.

00:05:49.449 --> 00:05:50.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
But it shows up
in the work you do,

00:05:50.983 --> 00:05:53.586 align:start size:94% position:6%
and I'm just so happy
to have you here.

